Types of System Compliance Documentation


regardless of which framework the organization uses, the documentation provided must include the level of detail necessary for a thorough review and analysis of how security and privacy controls align with the organizations risk management strategy and risk appetite


if the controls are not found to be satisfactory, the authorization package must have a plan of action and milestones (POA&M) document with a timeline for corrective and preventative activities for treatment of risk


some common types of system compliance documentation are: 

system security plan: this document describes the systems security objectives, controls, and procedures

system configuration guide: this document provides instructions on how to configure the systems hardware, software, and network settings

system test plan: this document outlines the testing methods, criteria, and results for verifying the systems functionality and compliance

system audit report: this document summarizes the findings and recommendations of an audit conducted on the system

system risk assessment: this document identifies and evaluates the potential threats and vulnerabilities that may affect the system

system contingency plan: this document defines the actions and resources needed to restore the systems operations in case of a disruption or disaster

system registry: this document provides an inventory of all systems within the enterprise architecture and a documented level of system compliance for these systems

compliance certification documents: independently evaluated and meets the requirements of a specific standard (e.g. ISO 27001, SOC 2). when a system undergoes certification against a specific standard, the resulting certification documents serve as proof of compliance.

plan of action and milestones (POA&M): this document outline the action plan for addressing any deficiencies in the systems security posture identified during security assessments or audits. it includes details about the vulnerability, proposed remedial actions, responsible individuals, and timelines for resolution. it is a dynamic document that track gross toward mitigating identified risks. 

training records: these documents describe security and compliance training programs and log the participation of employees. training records demonstrate that staff are aware of and understand their roles and responsibilities in maintaining system security and compliance

incident response and breach notification records: these documents outline how security incidents and data breaches are handled and reported for the system, including incident response plans, reports of incident investigations, and records of any breach notification sent to affected parties or regulatory bodies. these records are essential for compliance with regulations that require incident reporting and management


