Residual Risk Determination



to determine the compliance of a system and the level to which the information is protected, the implemented security and privacy controls should have verified and validated evidence.


the security and privacy plans, along with implementation guidelines and procedures, provide a level of verification and validation. when going through a structured risk management framework, the security and privacy assessments will provide documentation that verifies the requirements. assessments also validate that the controls sufficiently and appropriately address the risk and compliance. during system compliance evaluation, the security and privacy assessments will be analyzed against the organizational and system risk assessments. this analysis will review the evidence that validates the controls against compliance to the organizations risk management strategy. the validated control will then determine the residual risk and the level of likelihood and impact that remains to the organization


task 1: test and verify controls

task 2: analyze residual likelihood and impact

task 3: compare residual risk with stakeholder risk tolerance

task 4: create risk acceptance decision

task 5: document and communicate residual risk


evaluating the residual risk of the system is crucial for determining the system risk acceptance and monitoring.


system risk acceptance is the process of deciding whether to accept, reject, or transfer the residual risk based on the risk tolerance and appetite of the system stakeholders. system risk monitoring is the process of measuring and reporting the performance and status of the controls and the changes in the system risk posture


to evaluate the residual risk of the system, the GRC professional should perform the following activities: test and verify the implementation and operation of the controls. analyze the residual likelihood and residual imp[act of the threats on the system assets, operations, and stakeholders. compare the residual risk with the risk tolerance and appetite of the system stakeholders. decide whether to accept, avoid, or transfer the residual risk. document and communicate the residual risk and the risk acceptance decision


the alignment of organizational risk tolerance toward the risk treatment and residual risk becomes the basis with which to determine system compliance. once all risk to the system and information has been handled within the parameters of the organizational risk management strategy, the system can be authorized to operate and move to production. this determination should be documented and communicated within the system registry, which provides an inventory of all systems and their statuses in the enterprise architecture


