Formal Notification of Compliance Decision



creating and maintain system compliance documentation is a continuous and collaborative process that involves system administrators, auditors, regulators, customers, and other stakeholders


system compliance documentation provides formal guidance to the handling of risk within the system and information

system authorization is the formal notification and approval of a systems compliance status by and authorized official to the system owner. system authorization can also be called accreditation, certification, or validation. system authorization can provide assurance that a system is operating within acceptable boundaries of the organizations risk tolerance, supporting the organizations mission



NIST and ISO have requirements to document system compliance. NIST 800-37 defines four types of authorization decisions that can be made by an authorizing official: authorize; the system is authorized to operate with an acceptable level of risk. authorize with conditions; the system is authorized to operate with a specified set of conditions or limitations that must be addressed or mitigated. deny; the system is not authorized to operate due to unacceptable risks or deficiencies. revoke; the systems authorization is withdrawn due to a significant change in the system or environment. 


ISO 270001 specifies the requirements and best practices for establishing, implementing, maintaining, and improving an ISMS. ISO 270001 can help organizations protect their information assets, comply with legal and regulatory obligations, and enhance their reputation trust. the authorization and determination of system compliance is governed within the ISMS requirements for continuous monitoring of systems. 


