Formal Notification Shared with Stakeholders



formal notification ensures the system complies with relevant standards and regulations and communicates its compliance status to relevant authorities and stakeholders


once the formal documentation is complete and the system compliance decision is determined, GRC professional must formally notify stakeholders regarding system compliance, significant updates, or critical decisions. this ensures all relevant parties are continually informed about the status, changes, or decisions that may impact the operation, security, or compliance of a system or organization. system compliance is essential for maintaining the security, reliability, and performance of the system and protecting the data and privacy of users and stakeholders. therefore, these stakeholders should be informed of any new systems authorized to operate within the organization


ISO 270001 and NIST 800-37 require formal notification of the system compliance status to the relevant stakeholders, such as the system owners, managers, auditors, regulators, and customers


an organization that implements an ISMS can obtain an ISO 270001 certification, which demonstrates that the organization has met the requirements of the standard and established a continuous improvement process. the certification process involves an external audit by and accredited certification body, which verifies the conformity and effectiveness of the ISMS


the formal notification criteria for system compliance within ISO 270001 are as follows: the organization must inform the certification body of any signification changes or events that may affect the ISMS, such as changes in the scope, objects, processes, risks, incidents, or legal obligations. the organization must provide the certification body with access to the ISMS documentation, records, and evidence, as well as the personnel and facilities involved in the ISMS, for purpose of conducting surveillance audits and recertification audits. the organization must communicate the results of the audits, including any nonconformities, corrective actions, and opportunities for improvement, to the relevant stakeholders, such as top management, the ISMS team, and the interested parties. the organization must display the ISO 270001 certificate and logo in a truthful and accurate manner and must not imply that the certification applies to activities or locations outside the scope of the ISMS. 

the formal notification criteria for system compliance within NIST 800-37 are as follows: the system owner must inform the authorizing official and the security team of any changes or events that may affect the systems security and risk posture, such as changes in functionality, architecture, environment, threats, vulnerabilities, or incidents. the system owner must provide the authorizing official and the security documentation, records, and evidence, as well as the system and the environment, for the purpose of conducting security assessments and audits. the system owner must communicate the results of the security assessments and audits, including any findings, recommendations, and remediation actions, to the relevant stakeholders, such as top management, system users, and oversight authorities. the system owner must transparently display the system authorization status and the implemented security control and must not imply that the system is authorized or compliant for activities or purposes that are outside the scope of the system and the information.


formal notification is important and beneficial for maintaining consistency of system compliance throughout the organization and stakeholders


